/-! A regular permutation representation of the simple group in the counterexample
of van Doorn, Judin, Monticone and Morrison. The two generator permutations
come from multiplication of unitary matrices over the field of nine elements.
Left and right transitivity and commutation certify regularity. Conjugacy
reductions and products of conjugates certify simplicity.

For reproducibility, encode a + b*i over the field of nine elements as
a + 3*b with i squared equal to minus one. The generators in row-major
order are (6,1,8; 1,3,5; 4,7,0) and (3,0,0; 0,7,7; 0,5,7).
The four regular actions and their inverses use thirteen bits per image,
starting at the least significant end. The distance and conjugacy-class
tables use five and four bits. All table properties used below are
verified independently in the kernel. -/

namespace Unitary6048

